From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: direct to display (experimental): frames drawn into a CAMetalLayer

What: with OMACVM_GL_DIRECT=1 (OmacVM.app: "Show directly on the
display", experimental, off by default) the view's layer is a CAMetalLayer
and the IOSurface present draws each frame with GL straight into one of
its drawables (their IOSurfaces bound as GL textures, once each) instead of
into surfaces of its own that a plain CALayer shows. The vsync queue,
pacing, colour tags, HDR / extra brightness kinds (half-float drawables),
the band below a guest a few rows shorter than the window and the
sublayers stay as they are; a drawable is presented where a surface was
set as the layer's contents. Drawables come from a queue of their own
(nextDrawable can wait); QEMU's thread takes the spare one without waiting
and treats "none yet" as all surfaces busy (the frame waits a refresh, as
before). No partial draws into drawables (each comes back holding an older
frame). Needs the vsync present and a Metal device (dlsym: Metal is not
linked into QEMU); GPU safe mode keeps the plain layer. A drawable GL
cannot draw into turns it off for the run (plain layer, one warning).
qemu.log: "cocoa: direct to display: on", and from Core Animation's own
status of the layer "the display shows the window itself" or "composited
by WindowServer (status ...)", once a minute how many frames went direct.

Why: macOS 27 shows a full-screen window on the display itself (no
WindowServer composite: it neither reads the frame nor writes its own
framebuffer) only when its layer is a CAMetalLayer and no other window
covers any part of it; a CALayer showing IOSurfaces is always composited,
whatever the surface's kind, tags or Core Animation's private switches.
sRGB tags, scaled modes, our own sublayers, half-float drawables and a
window over the menu-bar strip (Omanotch's) keep it direct; any window over
the VM's window (a 1x1 pt one is enough) composites again.
Measured on a MacBook Air M2 (macOS 27.0.1, its scaled default mode, the
real VM full screen at 60 Hz, on/off/on/off, the same frame rates and
pixels): shown directly, WindowServer 0 vs 58-113 GPU ms/s and 13-24 % vs
22-41 % CPU, but the whole Mac no lower (scrolling 4.29 vs 4.27 W, 1080p30
video 3.85 vs 3.79 W, pointer 3.58 vs 3.44 W): GL can only draw into plain
drawables (lossless-compressed ones refuse a GL binding), so QEMU's draw
and the display's read move the bytes WindowServer's composite of the
lossless surfaces saved. Hence experimental and off: where the composite
costs more (half-float HDR frames at 120 Hz on an XDR display) it is not
measured yet.

Upstream: OmacVM only (QEMU's IOSurface present is OmacVM's).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-present-direct.sh (the wiring of the
patched ui/cocoa.m; the checks catch code without it). work/direct-display
(ddbench, the Air rows) for the numbers.
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-present-lossless.patch (before omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch).
